
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Internal Root CA – Installation Guide</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif;
            background: linear-gradient(145deg, #f0f4fa 0%, #e6edf4 100%);
            padding: 2rem;
            color: #1e2a3a;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 1300px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
            backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
            border-radius: 2rem;
            box-shadow: 0 25px 45px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .download-banner {
            background: #0f2b3d;
            color: white;
            padding: 1.2rem 2rem;
            text-align: center;
            border-bottom: 3px solid #2c7da0;
        }
        .download-banner h2 {
            margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
            color: white;
            border-left: none;
            font-size: 1.5rem;
        }
        .download-btn {
            display: inline-block;
            background: #2c7da0;
            color: white;
            padding: 0.6rem 1.5rem;
            border-radius: 40px;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: bold;
            margin-top: 0.5rem;
            transition: 0.2s;
            border: 1px solid #61a5c2;
        }
        .download-btn:hover {
            background: #1f5e7e;
            transform: scale(1.02);
        }

        .tabs {
            display: flex;
            background: #ffffffcc;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
            padding: 0 1.5rem;
            gap: 0.25rem;
        }

        .tab-button {
            background: transparent;
            border: none;
            padding: 1rem 1.8rem;
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #334155;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: 0.2s;
            border-radius: 1rem 1rem 0 0;
            margin-bottom: -1px;
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.6rem;
        }

        .tab-button:hover {
            background: #e9eef3;
            color: #0f172a;
        }

        .tab-button.active {
            background: #ffffff;
            color: #0f2b3d;
            border-bottom: 3px solid #2c7da0;
            font-weight: 700;
        }

        .tab-content {
            display: none;
            padding: 2rem 2rem 2.5rem 2rem;
            animation: fadeIn 0.25s ease;
        }

        .tab-content.active {
            display: block;
        }

        @keyframes fadeIn {
            from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(6px);}
            to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0);}
        }

        h2 {
            font-size: 1.8rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #0c4a6e;
            border-left: 6px solid #2c7da0;
            padding-left: 1rem;
        }

        h3 {
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            margin: 1.5rem 0 0.8rem 0;
            color: #1e4a6b;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        code {
            background: #1e293b;
            color: #e2e8f0;
            padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;
            border-radius: 8px;
            font-family: 'Fira Code', 'Cascadia Code', monospace;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }

        pre {
            background: #0f172a;
            color: #e2e8f0;
            padding: 1rem;
            border-radius: 1rem;
            overflow-x: auto;
            margin: 1rem 0;
            font-family: 'Fira Code', monospace;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            line-height: 1.45;
        }

        pre code {
            background: none;
            padding: 0;
        }

        .note {
            background: #fef9e3;
            border-left: 4px solid #f3b33d;
            padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
            margin: 1.2rem 0;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        .warning {
            background: #fee2e2;
            border-left: 4px solid #dc2626;
            padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
            margin: 1.2rem 0;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        .success {
            background: #e0f2fe;
            border-left: 4px solid #0891b2;
            padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
            margin: 1.2rem 0;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        .inline-code {
            background: #e9ecef;
            color: #b91c1c;
            padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;
            border-radius: 6px;
            font-family: monospace;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }

        ul, ol {
            margin: 0.6rem 0 0.8rem 1.8rem;
        }

        li {
            margin: 0.3rem 0;
        }

        hr {
            margin: 1.2rem 0;
            border: 0;
            height: 1px;
            background: #cbd5e1;
        }

        @media (max-width: 680px) {
            body { padding: 1rem; }
            .tab-button { padding: 0.7rem 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
            .tab-content { padding: 1.2rem; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
    <div class="download-banner">
        <h2>📜 Internal Root CA Certificate</h2>
        <p>Download the PEM certificate to install it on your system using the guides below.</p>
        <a href="/rootCA.pem" download="rootCA.pem" class="download-btn">⬇️ Download rootCA.pem</a>
    </div>

    <div class="tabs">
        <button class="tab-button active" data-tab="windows">🪟 Windows (GUI & CMD)</button>
        <button class="tab-button" data-tab="debian">🐧 Debian / Ubuntu</button>
        <button class="tab-button" data-tab="rhel">🔴 RHEL / CentOS / Fedora</button>
    </div>

    <!-- Windows Tab -->
    <div id="windows" class="tab-content active">
        <h2>📁 Windows – Import Root CA (Force overwrite)</h2>
        <p>Use the <strong>Local Machine</strong> certificate store to trust the CA system‑wide. Administrator rights are mandatory.</p>

        <h3>📌 Method 1: Graphical interface (recommended)</h3>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Download the certificate</strong><br>
                Use the button above or open <code class="inline-code">http://ca.localdomain/rootCA.pem</code> → save as <code class="inline-code">rootCA.crt</code> (rename extension to .crt).</li>
            <li><strong>Open Local Machine certificate store</strong><br>
                Press <code class="inline-code">Win + R</code>, type <code class="inline-code">certlm.msc</code> and press <strong>Enter</strong> (accept UAC).</li>
            <li><strong>Remove old certificate (force overwrite)</strong><br>
                Expand <code class="inline-code">Trusted Root Certification Authorities</code> → <code class="inline-code">Certificates</code>. Find your old root → right‑click → <strong>Delete</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Import new certificate</strong><br>
                Right‑click <code class="inline-code">Trusted Root Certification Authorities</code> → <strong>All Tasks</strong> → <strong>Import</strong> → browse to <code class="inline-code">rootCA.crt</code> → next → verify store → finish.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="note">📘 Using <code class="inline-code">certlm.msc</code> ensures installation for <strong>all users</strong>. Avoid double‑clicking a .crt file (current user only).</div>

        <h3>🖥️ Method 2: PowerShell (as Administrator)</h3>
        <pre><code># Force overwrite root CA from HTTP
$url = "http://ca.localdomain/rootCA.pem"
$storeLoc = "Cert:\LocalMachine\Root"
$tempPem = "$env:TEMP\rootCA_temp.pem"
$tempDer = "$env:TEMP\rootCA_temp.der"

Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $url -OutFile $tempPem
certutil -decode $tempPem $tempDer | Out-Null
$cert = New-Object System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates.X509Certificate2($tempDer)
$serial = $cert.GetSerialNumberString()

certutil -delstore Root $serial 2>$null
certutil -addstore Root $tempDer

Remove-Item $tempPem, $tempDer -Force
Write-Host "Root CA imported successfully" -ForegroundColor Green</code></pre>
        <div class="warning">⚠️ <strong>Admin required</strong>: Right‑click PowerShell → Run as Administrator.</div>

        <h3>🔒 Clearing HSTS settings (after root CA renewal)</h3>
        <p>If you have previously accessed the internal domain over HTTPS and the server sent a <code>Strict-Transport-Security</code> header, your browser may have cached HSTS policy for that domain. After replacing the root CA, you must clear this cache to avoid connection errors.</p>

        <h4>For Chromium‑based browsers (Chrome, Edge, Brave, etc.)</h4>
        <ol>
            <li>Type <code class="inline-code">chrome://net-internals/#hsts</code> (or <code class="inline-code">edge://net-internals/#hsts</code>).</li>
            <li>In the <strong>Delete domain security policies</strong> section, enter your internal domain (e.g. <code class="inline-code">ca.localdomain</code>) and click <strong>Delete</strong>.</li>
            <li>If you want to disable HSTS entirely for testing, you can also add the domain to the <strong>Delete domain security policies</strong> area – this removes any pinned HPKP and HSTS settings.</li>
        </ol>

        <h4>For Firefox</h4>
        <ol>
            <li>Type <code class="inline-code">about:config</code> in the address bar and accept the risk.</li>
            <li>Search for <code class="inline-code">strict</code> or directly for your domain. Alternatively, go to <strong>Settings → Privacy & Security → Cookies and Site Data → Manage Data</strong> and remove the entry for your internal domain.</li>
            <li>For HSTS specific, use the <strong>Site Security Service</strong> viewer: go to <code class="inline-code">about:networking#hsts</code>, then under <strong>Delete HSTS</strong> enter your domain and click <strong>Delete</strong>.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="note">📘 <strong>Why clear HSTS?</strong> After you change the root CA, the new certificate chain may differ (e.g., new public key). Browsers that previously recorded HSTS for the old certificate may refuse to connect. Clearing HSTS forces the browser to re‑evaluate the site’s security policy with the newly trusted CA.</div>

        <div class="success">✅ After importing the certificate and clearing HSTS (if needed), restart your browser completely. The internal site should now be trusted.</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Debian / Ubuntu Tab -->
    <div id="debian" class="tab-content">
        <h2>🐧 Debian, Ubuntu, and derivatives</h2>
        <p>System‑wide trust store using <code>update-ca-certificates</code>.</p>

        <h3>📥 1. Download and place certificate</h3>
        <pre><code>sudo wget -O /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/rootCA.crt http://ca.localdomain/rootCA.pem</code></pre>
        <div class="note">📌 Extension <strong>must be .crt</strong> and PEM format (<code>-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----</code>).</div>

        <h3>🔄 2. Update and force overwrite</h3>
        <pre><code>sudo update-ca-certificates --fresh</code></pre>
        <p>Or standard update (also overwrites):</p>
        <pre><code>sudo update-ca-certificates</code></pre>

        <h3>🧪 3. Verification</h3>
        <pre><code>trust list | grep -i "your CA name"   # if p11-kit installed</code></pre>

        <div class="success">✅ Reboot or restart services for full effect.</div>
    </div>

    <!-- RedHat / RHEL tab -->
    <div id="rhel" class="tab-content">
        <h2>🔴 RHEL, CentOS, Fedora, Rocky Linux, AlmaLinux</h2>
        <p>RedHat‑based distributions use <code>update-ca-trust</code>.</p>

        <h3>📥 1. Add certificate to anchors directory</h3>
        <pre><code>sudo wget -O /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/rootCA.crt http://ca.localdomain/rootCA.pem</code></pre>

        <h3>⚙️ 2. Rebuild trust store (force overwrite)</h3>
        <pre><code>sudo update-ca-trust extract</code></pre>
        <div class="warning">💡 To ensure a clean overwrite, remove the old bundle first:
            <pre><code>sudo rm -f /etc/pki/ca-trust/extracted/pem/tls-ca-bundle.pem
sudo update-ca-trust extract</code></pre>
        </div>

        <h3>✔️ 3. Verification</h3>
        <pre><code>openssl x509 -in /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/rootCA.crt -noout -subject
grep -A1 "YourCACommonName" /etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt</code></pre>

        <div class="note">📘 Alternatively, use <code>sudo trust anchor --store rootCA.pem</code> (p11-kit).</div>
        <div class="success">✅ Reboot to ensure all daemons pick up the new CA.</div>
    </div>
</div>

<script>
    const tabs = document.querySelectorAll('.tab-button');
    const contents = document.querySelectorAll('.tab-content');

    function activateTab(tabId) {
        contents.forEach(content => content.classList.remove('active'));
        const activeContent = document.getElementById(tabId);
        if (activeContent) activeContent.classList.add('active');

        tabs.forEach(btn => {
            btn.classList.remove('active');
            if (btn.getAttribute('data-tab') === tabId) btn.classList.add('active');
        });
        localStorage.setItem('lastRootCATab', tabId);
    }

    tabs.forEach(btn => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => activateTab(btn.getAttribute('data-tab')));
    });

    const lastTab = localStorage.getItem('lastRootCATab');
    if (lastTab && ['windows', 'debian', 'rhel'].includes(lastTab)) activateTab(lastTab);
</script>
</body>
</html>
